es is empty, if qty is negative, or if unit_price is negative. Unparseable price and non-int or bool qty presumably still raise ValueError. qty 0 is allowed and that line is skipped entirely.\n  - Superseded stage-2 rule: qty had to be a positive int.\n- Stage 3 NEW, format_money: prefix 'NZD' -> 'NZ$', 'AUD' -> 'A$', 'USD' -> 'US$'. Always 2 decimals. A negative amount puts '-' before the prefix (e.g. '-NZ$5.00'). Any other currency raises ValueError.\n  - Already implemented; it uses r2 with half-up rounding.\n\nCurrent code (core.py), stage-3 state\n- `r2` quantizes with ROUND_HALF_UP.\n- `TIER_RATES` holds the stage-2 rates.\n- `line_amount` applies the bulk factor, then calls r2.\n- `discount_rate` and `tax_rate` (fixed 0.10).\n- `validate` rejects q <= 0.\n- `compute_invoice` uses r2 throughout.\n- `PREFIX` dict and `format_money`.\n- NOTES.md is appended per stage.\n\nStatus\n- Stage 2: 10/10 tests passed. Stage 3: 12/12 tests passed.\n\nRemaining stage-4 work\n- Make line_amount return the unrounded amount.\n- Add a half-even rounding helper.\n- compute_invoice:\n  - skip qty == 0 lines;\n  - compute exact subtotal, discount and tax;\n  - set tax to 0 if tax_exempt is True;\n  - round each value half-even;\n  - total = sum of the rounded values.\n- validate: allow 0 and reject negative qty (keep int/bool checks).\n- Keep format_money on half-up rounding.\n- Run tests, update NOTES.md, then submit the final answer."
